const pertDraft = pancreaticLivingTermDrafts.find((t) => t.id === PERT_DRAFT_ID);

/**
 * PANCREATIC CANCER: the core layer of the six-file deep dive (24 Sept 2026), written to the standard of the gallbladder
 * and triple-negative files (docs/GALLBLADDER-QA.md, docs/TNBC-QA.md). The cancer record `pancreatic` lives in
 * ../cancers.ts and is already patched by ./pancreatic.ts (trials, drugs, treatment rows, history, pipeline). This file
 * PATCHES it again (cancerId "pancreatic"): epidemiology (world, UK, US), the rising incidence, age and risk factors,
 * presentation and the late-diagnosis problem, diagnosis and staging (pancreas protocol CT, EUS sampling, the
 * resectability classes, TNM 8th edition), pathology and precursor lesions, screening and surveillance, outlook figures
 * and the FAQ. Patches merge in registration order and scalars override, so the `summary` written in ./pancreatic.ts is
 * carried over verbatim at the top of the new summary (edit it here, not there); the treatment rows, history entries
 * and pipeline of ./pancreatic.ts and the stage, driver and histology pages of ../pancreatic-subtypes.ts are left alone.
 *
 * The record `pancreatic` is named "Pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma" and is the entity most people mean by pancreatic
 * cancer, so no separate ductal adenocarcinoma page is created (it would duplicate the record); the aka list gains the
 * plain names instead. Pancreatic neuroendocrine tumours already exist (`pancreatic-net`, neuroendocrine spike) and are
 * linked, not duplicated. Acinar cell carcinoma, IPMN and the cystic precursors, and pancreatoblastoma already exist in
 * ../pancreatic-subtypes.ts and are linked, not rewritten.
 *
 *   subtypes (parent pancreatic)  pancreatic-adenosquamous-carcinoma, pancreatic-colloid-carcinoma,
 *                                 pancreatic-undifferentiated-carcinoma-ogc (osteoclast-like giant cells),
 *                                 ipmn-associated-carcinoma, mcn-associated-carcinoma, solid-pseudopapillary-neoplasm
 *   terms                         nccn-resectability-criteria-pancreatic, pancreas-protocol-ct, distal-pancreatectomy,
 *                                 vascular-resection-pancreatic, pancreatic-enzyme-replacement, lewis-negative, panin,
 *                                 pancreatic-cyst-high-risk-stigmata, new-onset-diabetes-pancreatic-cancer,
 *                                 r0-r1-margin-pancreatic, neoadjuvant-versus-upfront-surgery-pancreatic,
 *                                 emergency-presentation, familial-pancreatic-cancer
 *   living-with terms             drafted in ./pancreatic-living.ts (pancreaticLivingTermDrafts) and registered from
 *                                 here after review: type-3c-diabetes-pancreatic-cancer, coeliac-plexus-block,
 *                                 eating-after-whipple, chemotherapy-side-effects-pancreatic, urgent-help-pancreatic-cancer,
 *                                 work-and-money-pancreatic-cancer-uk, carers-pancreatic-cancer-uk; the eighth draft
 *                                 (pert-pancreatic-cancer) is folded into pancreatic-enzyme-replacement
 *   supplements                   whipple, ca19-9, cachexia, resection-margins, resectability (pancreatic notes and
 *                                 sources added to the existing glossary terms)
 *
 * Existing ids reused rather than duplicated: whipple (Whipple procedure), resectability (resectable, borderline
 * resectable, unresectable, with "borderline resectable" and "upfront surgery" as aliases), locally-advanced,
 * resection-margins (R0, R1, R2), neoadjuvant-adjuvant, cachexia, ca19-9, desmoplasia, obstructive-jaundice,
 * pancreatic-surveillance (technology), precede (trial), ipmn-cystic-precursors (whose aliases are IPMN, MCN and
 * pancreatic cyst), borderline-resectable-pdac and locally-advanced-pdac (setting pages kept for their URLs).
 *
 * Subtype standard-of-care rows reference regimens and glossary terms, not trial ids: a trial with posted outcomes that a
 * cancer references gains a section on /explained/ (src/lib/explained-data.ts), and six new sections for PRODIGE 24
 * pushed that page past its 640 KB budget (src/app/heavy-pages.test.ts). The parent record carries the trials.
 *
 * Every figure is quoted from the page or abstract named beside it: Cancer Research UK statistics and patient pages,
 * NHS pages, SEER Cancer Stat Facts (pancreatic cancer), the GLOBOCAN pancreas fact sheet (2024 estimates, read 24 Sept
 * 2026), NICE NG85 and NG12, and papers read through the Europe PMC REST API (cached under /tmp/panc). Where sources
 * disagree (Cancer Research UK gives 37 percent preventable on its summary page and 31 percent on its risk page) both are
 * recorded.
 */
